  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Composure as a Marker of Superiority",
  "description": "This stereotype suggests that Black people are inherently more composed or professional, which is used to imply they are 'too good' to be wild or uninhibited. This is a harmful trope that reinforces racial hierarchies by suggesting that Black people are naturally more restrained, which is not true and is used to demean or stereotype them.",
